# taken from NIST Circuit Complexity:
# https://github.com/usnistgov/Circuits/blob/master/data/slp/aes/aes-sbox-rev-g127-a34-d16-ad4.slp
# NIST project listing:
# https://github.com/usnistgov/Circuits/blob/master/data/slp/aes/README.md
# AES specification:
# https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.FIPS.197-upd1
#
# The NIST source SLP does not cite a separate circuit-design paper.
# This file implements the inverse AES S-box (InvSubBytes), not the forward S-box.
#
# normalized interface: x0..x7 / s0..s7, index 0 = AES byte MSB.
#
# Unrail results:
# NL: total=34, DR=16, DR2SR_B2F=18
# L:  total=93, DR=56, SR_F2B=0, SR_B2F=37
# REG=8
#
# #gates:     127
# depth (NL):  16 (4)
# #L:          93
# #NL:         34
